        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "56d715a1-6b2b-5035-bb93-6e7c07b17ad9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Ghostkeeper, Lonesome Dove: The Series\n- People: Jim Makichuk, Georgie Collins\n- Concepts: Windigo legend, Wendigo psychosis\n- Topics: Canadian independent horror, culture-bound syndrome\n\nFacts:\n- Ghostkeeper is a 1981 Canadian independent horror film directed by Jim Makichuk.\n- The plot of Ghostkeeper is inspired by the Windigo legend of North America.\n- Georgie Collins is known for her role in the 1981 cult horror film Ghostkeeper.\n- Wendigo psychosis is a controversial modern medical term derived from the Wendigo legend.\n- Psychiatrists have described Wendigo psychosis as a culture-bound syndrome marked by an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.\n- Georgie Collins also appeared in Lonesome Dove: The Series in 1995.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
